 ## Overview
-Hierarchical sampling (Inverse CDF Sampling) is a method for generating importance samples along a ray in volume rendering by inverting the cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the rendering contribution [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently placing sample points in regions of high density without redundant radiance queries [S4, S5, S6, unofficial]. Unlike uniform ray sampling, this method concentrates fine samples where the coarse pass indicated high opacity [G]. It builds on [Sampling and Jittering](2516-sampling-and-jittering.md) by providing a deterministic or stratified mechanism to draw from a discrete probability distribution defined by per-bin weights [S1, S3, unofficial].
